{"id": "EUVD-2026-49603", "enisaUuid": "9cba6725-545c-322b-871f-2a196bb0df2f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvirtio-net: fix len check in receive_big()\n\nreceive_big() bounds the device-announced length by\n(big_packets_num_skbfrags + 1) * PAGE_SIZE.  That is still too loose:\nadd_recvbuf_big() sets sg[1] to start at offset\nsizeof(struct padded_vnet_hdr) into the first page, so the chain\nactually carries hdr_len + (PAGE_SIZE - sizeof(padded_vnet_hdr)) +\nbig_packets_num_skbfrags * PAGE_SIZE bytes -- 20 bytes less than the\ncheck allows for the common hdr_len == 12 case.\n\nA malicious virtio backend can announce a len in that gap.  page_to_skb()\nthen walks one frag past the page chain, storing a NULL page->private\ninto skb_shinfo()->frags[MAX_SKB_FRAGS], which is both an out-of-bounds\nwrite past the static frag array and a NULL frag handed up the rx path.\n\nBound len by the size add_recvbuf_big() actually advertised.", "datePublished": "2026-07-27T20:10:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:40", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9451d0fd5ba635dcabb49bfe456a6db734a8986", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38e94d63e29f4a5c6eae87ee2c02101aaa321502", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fbeb65154583879d556ea94cb2f15888e9470f3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c7fc9adf4e006155f7f2aeda052fbcde25cdcc49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6b8463b7d791f3886d7584259d6e9f06a69f12e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e5ad06ea826322ce8c58b4a68442a96f600c3c4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64552", "GHSA-6c34-77j2-7g8c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "057077bc-477c-33e2-aa05-5ca64a3c1646", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "946dec89c41726b94d31147ec528b96af0be1b5a <38e94d63e29f4a5c6eae87ee2c02101aaa321502"}, {"id": "09b52717-d4bc-338e-897c-ac2857eba658", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82fe78065450d2d07f36a22e2b6b44955cf5ca5b <fbeb65154583879d556ea94cb2f15888e9470f3d"}, {"id": "194a325f-5268-338a-a3ea-1c0e8c1c785b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c716703965ffc5ef4311b65cb5d84a703784717 <e6b8463b7d791f3886d7584259d6e9f06a69f12e"}, {"id": "1e8480ea-942c-3d64-b3be-467d00e4ecec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "2d87626f-e021-38f1-b96e-4f1f7468cfa6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "403a77fd-c75b-3950-81db-eb70bcc90e89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f9028e83944a9eee5229cbc6fee9be1de8a62d <f9451d0fd5ba635dcabb49bfe456a6db734a8986"}, {"id": "4b937b60-2393-3eed-8a1d-08abb85a3f77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "766c4967-84d0-3b53-bc55-3e5aa65edf82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.117 <6.6.145"}, {"id": "777baa23-cedf-36c1-a1f7-df9dd4f96058", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "7ecf3290-7b91-3aeb-87f0-0bafa8042c39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "8dde3bef-751e-3f8a-9e70-58ca3342989f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.159 <6.1.178"}, {"id": "9cd64097-45e5-3879-8b4d-f6d0c5438063", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c716703965ffc5ef4311b65cb5d84a703784717 <c7fc9adf4e006155f7f2aeda052fbcde25cdcc49"}, {"id": "ad94d0e3-6097-33cb-b1b9-12c1f5cc2a53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "af9e7676-c878-3656-b7